%% param_free_not_checked.glp — NEGATIVE guard, case (ii) of the abstract-parameter
%% routing matrix (parameterized-types.tex sec:abstract-parameters; spec:
%% docs/type system/typed-program.md "Modular Checking via Abstract Parameters").
%%
%% (Filename retained for continuity; the behaviour it guards has changed — see
%% below. A rename to param_abstract_gap.glp is a reasonable follow-up.)
%%
%% pdrop/1 is a parameterized procedure that does NOT inspect its parameter (the
%% element position holds the anonymous variable `_`, not a functor/constant) and
%% does not use its parameter as a type-definition alternative.  It therefore takes
%% the ABSTRACT ROUTE: it is checked once against its abstract instance
%% pdrop(Stream<$abstract_X>?), by def:parametrically-well-typed — clauses
%% well-typed AND every input path covered.
%%
%% pdrop has a COVERAGE GAP: no clause for the empty stream [].  The abstract-route
%% check runs contravariance against Stream<$abstract_X>? and finds [] uncovered,
%% so pdrop is not parametrically well-typed and is left to be checked per
%% instantiation.  No call instantiates it, so the file is REJECTED: "Where a
%% program contains a parameterised procedure that no call in it instantiates and
%% that is not parametrically well-typed, compilation rejects the program"
%% (sec:abstract-parameters).  The refusal quotes the abstract instance's error.
%%
%% Contrast with the previous semantics, under which a free-parameter procedure was
%% "not a program" and went unchecked (the old positive behaviour this file once
%% guarded).  Paired with param_instantiated_coverage_gap.glp (same pdrop, also
%% rejected) and with the positive case param_abstract_covered.glp (clean, covered,
%% certified clean).
%%
%% Run (from /Users/udi/Grassroots/GLP/glp_runtime/):
%%   printf 'load ../programs/tests/param_free_not_checked.glp\n:quit\n' | bin/glpc

procedure(X) pdrop(Stream(X)?).
pdrop([_|Xs]) :- pdrop(Xs?).
